  "readmeFile": "docs\\README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0 — Breaking Changes\n\n• Entire public API is now async. All methods return Task and follow the Async suffix naming convention.\n  - Factory: CreateSdk() → CreateSdkAsync() returning Task<IBadHareDataCradleSdk>\n  - Publisher: Publish(), PublishCardDrawn(), etc. → PublishAsync(), PublishCardDrawnAsync(), etc.\n  - Subscriber: SubscribeCardDrawn(), Ready(), etc. → SubscribeCardDrawnAsync(), ReadyAsync(), etc.\n• Upgraded to RabbitMQ.Client 7.x — IModel replaced with IChannel; all channel operations are natively async.\n• Upgraded to MessagePack 3.x.\n• No more sync-over-async (GetAwaiter().GetResult()) anywhere in the SDK.\n\nNew Message Types:\n• DcDeviceHealthItem — subscribe to and publish device health telemetry.\n• DcManagementActionItem — subscribe to and publish management action commands.\n\nMigration from v1.x:\n  Callers must await all SDK calls and update method names to their Async equivalents. The factory now returns a Task so SDK creation must also be awaited.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "verbatimVersion": "2.0.0-beta1",
